+# Epic Breakdown: Pulseboard
+
+**Project**: Pulseboard  
+**Date**: 2026-08-10  
+**Total Epics**: 4 (E000 plus 3 product epics)  
+**Estimated Total Stories**: 12–18
+
+---
+
+## Planning Boundary
+
+This Build-level plan intentionally contains no more than three product epics. It preserves each product-contract promise without adding recording, calendar replacement, autonomous messaging, market, pricing, or provider-selection scope.
+
+## Epic Dependency Map
+
+```text
+E000 Developer Infrastructure
+  └── E001 Secure Transcript Intake
+        └── E002 Reviewed Action Items
+              └── E003 Reminder Delivery
+```
+
+## Epic Prioritization
+
+### Pilot MVP Epics
+
+- E000: Developer Infrastructure
+- E001: Secure Transcript Intake
+- E002: Reviewed Action Items
+- E003: Reminder Delivery
+
+### Enhancement and Future Epics
+
+None are planned. The four-week pilot is bounded to the above complete facilitator path.
+
+## Epic Definitions
+
+### E000: Developer Infrastructure
+
+**Value Statement**: Establish a reliable delivery foundation so the two-engineer pilot can test, deploy, and investigate the production path safely.
+
+**Scope Summary**: Configure local test execution, CI checks, environment/secrets conventions, and a deploy path appropriate to the Python API and browser UI. Configure production issue visibility or document a lightweight equivalent suitable for the pilot.
+
+**Success Criteria**:
+
+- [ ] Tests can run locally with a single documented command.
+- [ ] CI runs applicable lint, test, and build checks for changes.
+- [ ] Runtime configuration and secrets are separated from source control.
+- [ ] A staging or pilot deployment path is documented and executable.
+
+**User Stories Summary**:
+
+- Test and quality-command foundation
+- CI pipeline for API and browser UI
+- Environment and secrets configuration
+- Deployment and production-observability baseline
+
+**Dependencies**:
+
+- **Depends On**: None.
+- **Enables**: E001, E002, E003.
+
+**Estimated Stories**: 3–4  
+**Priority**: P0 — Foundation  
+**Target Phase**: Phase 0
+
+### E001: Secure Transcript Intake
+
+**Value Statement**: Enable a facilitator to upload a transcript into the correct workspace and receive proposed action items without exposing workspace data to another tenant.
+
+**Scope Summary**: Establish the workspace-scoped data and request path for transcript upload and extraction of proposed actions. Include the authorization mechanism and the negative isolation proof needed for PRM-004; do not schedule or send reminders in this epic.
+
+**Success Criteria**:
+
+- [ ] A facilitator can upload a transcript into a workspace.
+- [ ] The system produces proposed action items from the uploaded transcript (PRM-001).
+- [ ] A request using the real request role cannot read another workspace's transcripts or actions (PRM-004).
+
+**User Stories Summary**:
+
+- Workspace membership and request-scoped authorization
+- Transcript upload and storage
+- Action-proposal extraction and persistence
+- Cross-workspace negative access probe
+
+**Dependencies**:
+
+- **Depends On**: E000.
+- **Enables**: E002, E003.
+
+**Estimated Stories**: 4–6  
+**Priority**: P0 — Pilot critical  
+**Target Phase**: Phase 1
+
+### E002: Reviewed Action Items
+
+**Value Statement**: Enable a facilitator to turn proposals into complete, explicitly approved actions so nothing is scheduled or sent without human judgment.
+
+**Scope Summary**: Provide the browser review flow for proposals created by E001. The flow requires a facilitator to confirm action text, owner, and due date before an action can become eligible for scheduling; it does not itself deliver reminders.
+
+**Success Criteria**:
+
+- [ ] A facilitator can review and edit a proposed action item.
+- [ ] An action cannot be scheduled until text, owner, and due date are explicitly confirmed (PRM-002).
+- [ ] Unconfirmed proposals cannot cause an outbound reminder.
+- [ ] The facilitator LARP can complete the review path with the confirmation boundary understood.
+
+**User Stories Summary**:
+
+- Proposal-review browser UI
+- Edit and explicit-confirm action details
+- Scheduling eligibility state and outbound guard
+- Pilot metric capture for proposal review
+
+**Dependencies**:
+
+- **Depends On**: E000, E001.
+- **Enables**: E003.
+
+**Estimated Stories**: 3–5  
+**Priority**: P0 — Pilot critical  
+**Target Phase**: Phase 2
+
+### E003: Reminder Delivery
+
+**Value Statement**: Enable a facilitator to send one reminder for a confirmed action and see its delivery status.
+
+**Scope Summary**: Add a configurable reminder-provider boundary and a delivery-status surface. It consumes only actions made eligible by E002, delivers one reminder, and reports the resulting status; selecting the specific provider is deferred to implementation.
+
+**Success Criteria**:
+
+- [ ] A configurable provider can be used to send one reminder for a confirmed action (PRM-003).
+- [ ] An unconfirmed action cannot be sent through the provider.
+- [ ] A facilitator can see delivery status for the reminder (PRM-003).
+- [ ] Runtime evidence exercises upload → confirmation → delivery.
+
+**User Stories Summary**:
+
+- Configurable reminder-provider contract
+- One-reminder scheduling and delivery invocation
+- Delivery-status persistence and browser UI
+- End-to-end runtime evidence across the facilitator path
+
+**Dependencies**:
+
+- **Depends On**: E000, E001, E002.
+- **Enables**: Pilot evaluation.
+
+**Estimated Stories**: 2–3  
+**Priority**: P0 — Pilot critical  
+**Target Phase**: Phase 3
+
+## Epic Execution Strategy
+
+### Phase 0: Delivery Foundation
+
+- **Epic**: E000
+- **Goal**: establish reliable local, CI, configuration, and deployment practices before product work.
+- **Success Gate**: relevant checks run and a pilot deployment path is available.
+
+### Phase 1: Secure Intake
+
+- **Epic**: E001
+- **Goal**: create the workspace-safe upload-to-proposal path.
+- **Success Gate**: proposals are created from uploads and real-role cross-workspace reads are denied.
+
+### Phase 2: Human-Controlled Review
+
+- **Epic**: E002
+- **Goal**: make the confirmation boundary clear and enforceable.
+- **Success Gate**: only confirmed text, owner, and due date can become eligible for delivery.
+
+### Phase 3: Reminder Outcome
+
+- **Epic**: E003
+- **Goal**: complete the facilitator path with one reminder and visible status.
+- **Success Gate**: runtime evidence covers upload → confirmation → delivery, plus facilitator LARP.
+
+## Risk Mitigation by Epic
+
+| Epic | Primary Risk | Mitigation Strategy |
+|---|---|---|
+| E000 | Pilot work cannot be checked or deployed reliably | Establish the smallest complete delivery baseline first |
+| E001 | Tenant data isolation fails | Request-scoped authorization and real-role negative probe |
+| E002 | Human confirmation is ambiguous or bypassable | Explicit field confirmation and outbound eligibility guard |
+| E003 | Provider choice or delivery failure obscures the outcome | Configurable provider boundary and surfaced delivery status |
+
+## Success Metrics by Epic
+
+| Epic | Key Metric | Target | Measurement |
+|---|---|---:|---|
+| E001 | Unauthorized cross-workspace reads | 0 successful reads | Real request-role negative probe |
+| E002 | Proposal review rate | ≥80% | Reviewed proposals ÷ proposed actions |
+| E003 | Pilot participation | 5 teams | Count pilot teams/workspaces |
+| E003 | Unowned overdue actions | 30% fewer | Agreed baseline comparison over four weeks |
+
+## Concurrency and Sequencing
+
+This Build plan has three product epics, so formal wave validation is not required. The slices are intentionally sequential: E001 owns the workspace-safe data path, E002 owns the human confirmation gate, and E003 consumes only confirmed actions. This avoids parallel changes to the same action and authorization boundaries during a four-week, two-engineer pilot.
+
+## Notes
+
+- Epic placeholders are drafts only; each must be specified before implementation.
+- Provider selection, identity solution, implementation stack details, and metric instrumentation remain reversible implementation decisions.
+- `/project-analyze` is recommended before the first `/epic-specify`; it is not a mandatory Build 1–3 gate.
